  triage:resolutionNote "Content-verified fixed on feature/ay3-herdr-endpoint-doctor-config: git show c8bfb76e3:crates/atm-herdr/src/transport_cli.rs shows spawn() now routed through a `server_unavailable(error: std::io::Error)` helper that sets `io_error_kind: Some(error.kind())` on HerdrError::ServerUnavailable, preserving the io::Error kind for doctor_probe.rs's BinaryNotFound/BinaryNotExecutable mapping; same content confirmed present at b8afa814f. This matches QA-AY3-R3 (PASS, 0/0/0, pin b8afa814f, result 01M1X94GT0NFEPJG6CGTRV2TGY) and QA-AY3-R4 (FAIL only on AY3-QA-002, pin c8bfb76e3, result 01M1XC8WH4Z9E6H1EZM4H6ZR0D) in docs/plans/phase-ay/.audit/qa-evidence-master.json. Finding-level status set to fixed_partial (not fixed), matching the AY2-QA-001 precedent: the fix has not merged to integrate/phase-ay (PR #1273 open, mergeable=MERGEABLE/mergeStateStatus=CLEAN as of this reconciliation) and the integrate/phase-ay occurrence (AY3-2, headSha 1770ac80e) remains genuinely open on the current codebase." .

